id: pm-irp1
title: "ADR: Startup-latency strategy (prebuilt JS, lazy per-command imports, external deps, no single bundle)"
description: "Cold-start is optimized via prebuilt JS, lazy per-command module imports, and external deps rather than a single bundled binary."
type: Decision
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: adr,architecture,"area:performance",startup
created_at: "2026-05-31T20:15:02.138Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T08:28:22.602Z"
author: maintainer-agent
parent: pm-m2u1
resolution: Accepted ADR recorded in living map
expected_result: "The ADR captures a durable architecture or operating decision with context, consequences, and evidence for future agents."
actual_result: "The closed Decision 'ADR: Startup-latency strategy (prebuilt JS, lazy per-command imports, external deps, no single bundle)' is recorded under the ADR living log and preserved as durable project context."
close_reason: ADR recorded and accepted; startup-latency strategy documented as durable context on 2026-05-31.
body: "CONTEXT: per-invocation latency is dominated by ESM module resolution, not compute; agents and humans invoke pm hundreds of times per session, so cold-start is a primary UX lever. This was captured only as delivery items (pm-gt82, pm-t57d, pm-ss1d), never as a decision record. DECISION: optimize cold-start by (1) shipping prebuilt JS so no transpile happens per invocation, (2) lazy-importing each command's own module through a thin dispatch layer in src/cli/main.ts rather than eagerly loading a single large command barrel, and (3) keeping node_modules external (esbuild --packages=external) because bundling dependencies was measured slower. CONSEQUENCES: fast cold-start for the common single-command invocation at the cost of a thin dispatch indirection; the package is not a single self-contained binary because deps remain external. EVIDENCE: src/cli/main.ts dispatch, the esbuild build config; delivery items pm-gt82 (esbuild bundling), pm-t57d (per-command code-splitting), pm-ss1d (ESM module-resolution overhead).\n\nFOLLOW-UP 2026-07-25 (pm-yse5dt): preserve the accepted prebuilt-JS and per-command lazy-dispatch strategy, and additionally gate transport cost as an explicit CLI-minus-SDK budget. One-item cold-process measurements now cover get/list/context/next/create/claim; 10,000-item scale reports retain independent CLI and SDK absolute budgets plus a measured delta ratchet. Focused SDK package entrypoints are independently bundled and measured so package authors load only the capability family they use. This refines observability and package import topology without adopting a single dependency-bundled binary."
